title: Economic Democracy
is-card: true
new-page: true
on-arrival: economic_democracy_timer += 8; month_actions += 1
view-if: pps_in_government and economic_minister_party == "PPS" or and labor_minister_party == "PPS" and economic_democracy_timer <= 0
card-image: img/portraits/KwapińskiJan.jpg
max-visits: 8
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet
#subtitle: How can we give workers more control over the means of production?

= Economic Democracy

A key part of the social democratic platform is that workers should have more control over the economy. This can be done either directly at the enterprise level, by giving works councils greater influence over management, or indirectly via the democratic government, by acquiring key industries from the capitalist class and placing them under democratic control.

[? if foreign_interest_industry > 1 : Currently, much of the <span style="color: #CCC;">Pol</span><span style="color: #DC143C;">and</span>'s economy is currently under control by <span style="color: #000000;">Ge</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">rm</span><span style="color: #FFCE00;">an</span> interest left by the post-partition. ?]

As we control the Labor [? if economic_minister_party == "SPD" : and Economic ?][? if finance_minister_party == "SPD" : and Finance ?] ministries, we can finally begin to implement our long-standing goals. [? if in_grand_coalition: Our bourgeois coalition partners might not agree, however. ?]

